# Template Conformance

Read `workflow-state.yaml` §`template` and [template-registry.md](../../skills/template-registry.md).

**Template**: `static+api+worker` — React frontend + FastAPI backend + auth middleware in
single API deployable + F8 Render Background Worker (`apps/worker/`). Amended by ADR-018.

## File Structure

Warn if new deployable or library code is created outside the approved monorepo tree:

```
apps/backend/            # FastAPI — conversion, validation, auth routes
apps/frontend/           # React/Vite static deployable
apps/worker/             # F8 near-RT ingest poller (Background Worker)
apps/e2e/                # Playwright cross-app tests
packages/auth/           # Supabase middleware library (not a deployable)
packages/tac2iwxxm/      # General TAC → IWXXM (F6); MIT; PyO3 at cutover
packages/tac-validate/   # TAC lint / business rules
packages/iwxxm-validate/ # XSD + Schematron (F2 engine)
packages/dissemination/  # F16–F19 sinks / writer-contract / SSRF helpers (ADR-030)
packages/shared/         # API types, env helpers, constants
packages/gifts/          # Transitional until F6 cutover PR deletes it
vendor/schemas/*         # Read-only wmo-im + iwxxm-us snapshots
```

Do **not** create:
- A separate auth deployable or `apps/auth/` service
- A dedicated converter microservice (HTTP convert stays on `apps/backend`)
- New top-level `backend/`, `frontend/`, `GIFTs/` directories (legacy — migrate, don't extend)
- Edits inside `vendor/schemas/*` except via sync PRs updating manifest pins

## Service Layout

| Archetype | This project |
|-----------|--------------|
| API | `apps/backend` — single HTTP service (conversion + validation + `/auth/*`) |
| Static | `apps/frontend` — Vite build → Render static site |
| Worker | `apps/worker` — Render Background Worker (F8 poller → store/quarantine) |

## Separation of Concerns

- **packages/tac2iwxxm**: IWXXM serialization only — no FastAPI/Supabase imports
- **packages/tac-validate** / **iwxxm-validate**: lint/validate engines — no FastAPI/Supabase
- **packages/dissemination**: sink adapters + writer-contract + SSRF helpers — no FastAPI/Supabase
- **packages/auth**: JWT middleware and auth routes — no conversion logic
- **apps/backend**: HTTP routers wiring tac2iwxxm + validate + auth (+ thin dissemination)
- **apps/worker**: ingest orchestration only — calls packages; writes via service-role JWT
- **vendor/schemas**: Consumed read-only — never edited locally
- **packages/gifts**: transitional only until cutover deletes it

## Env Wiring

- Frontend: runtime `/config.json` (or build-time `VITE_API_BASE_URL`) → single API host
  (includes `/auth/*`)
- Backend runtime: `METAR_CORS_ORIGINS` / `config.*.api.corsOrigins` for browser origins
- Worker runtime: poller URL + Supabase service-role credentials (no browser CORS)

Surface `[Template Drift]` via AskQuestion if code diverges from these patterns without an ADR.
